{
  "_readme": "Source of truth for every Aurion sound. `sound` is an id from `earshot sounds`; `want` is a plain-language request. Layer fields: sound, want, seed, dur, pitch, theme, voice, events, the earshot axes (bright hard ring size space width energy motion, -1..1), plus mix fields handled by ffmpeg: at (s), gain (dB), start/trim (s), fade_in/fade_out (s), lowpass/highpass (Hz), pan (-1..1). `notes: [[pitch, at, gainDb?], ...]` repeats a layer once per note. Item fields: id, volume (manifest base volume), stereo, trim, fade_out, peak (dBFS ceiling), minIntervalMs (throttle), and for loops: loop, length (s), lufs. See generate.py.",
  "defaults": {
    "seed": 7,
    "peak": -3,
    "music_lufs": -20,
    "bitrates": { "sfx_mono": [48, 64], "sfx_stereo": [64, 96], "music": [64, 64] }
  },
  "sounds": [
